text:
This page provides an exploratory analysis of the combined Irish tide-gauge dataset containing observations from the Marine Institute (MI) and the Office of Public Works (OPW).
The purpose of this stage is to understand the observational data available before any tidal harmonic or statistical modelling is performed. In particular, the analysis examines:

the stations and observations contributed by MI and OPW;
the spatial and temporal coverage of the combined network;
sampling frequencies and changes in recording frequency;
gaps and completeness of the time series;
the distribution and range of observed water levels;
quality-control information;
station metadata, including coordinates and datum information; and
which stations have sufficient data for the subsequent tidal analysis.

Importantly, the duration of a station record and its completeness are treated as separate properties. A station may span several years while still containing substantial periods of missing observations. The annual completeness summaries therefore provide additional information that should be considered when constructing the three-year, five-year and longer analysis windows used later in the project.
At this stage no observations are inserted to fill gaps, no missing water levels are predicted, and no tidal harmonic models are fitted. Those steps belong to the subsequent data-processing and tidal-analysis stages.
The outputs from this page provide the basis for deciding which observations and stations should proceed to that analysis.


Show code
library(arrow)
library(tidyverse)
library(lubridate)
library(patchwork)

here::i_am("index.qmd")

theme_set(
  theme_bw() +
    theme(legend.position = "top", legend.direction = "horizontal"))

dir.create(here::here("outputs"), recursive = TRUE, showWarnings = FALSE)
dir.create(here::here("rds"), recursive = TRUE, showWarnings = FALSE)




Show code
fl &lt;- here::here("data", "merged_tide_gauge_data", "iteration_a_qc1")
da_arrow &lt;- open_dataset(fl, format = "parquet")


The analysis below uses the combined quality-controlled dataset. Therefore, unless otherwise stated, all observations shown on this page have already passed the QC procedure.


Show code
vars_required &lt;- c("time", "station_id", "st_id", "latitude", "longitude", "Water_Level_OD_Malin", "QC_Flag")
vars_optional &lt;- c("source", "data_source", "provider", "network", "source_station_code", "source_station_id", "datum", "datum_status")

vars_keep &lt;- intersect(c(vars_required, vars_optional), names(da_arrow))

da &lt;- da_arrow |&gt;
  select(all_of(vars_keep)) |&gt;
  collect()

if (!"st_id" %in% names(da)) {
  da &lt;- da |&gt;
    mutate(st_id = gsub(" ", "", station_id))
}

source_candidates &lt;- c("source", "data_source", "provider", "network")
source_col &lt;- source_candidates[source_candidates %in% names(da)][1]

if (is.na(source_col)) {
  stop(paste0("No MI/OPW source column was found. ", "Expected one of: ", paste(source_candidates, collapse = ", "), ". Add the appropriate source column name to source_candidates."))
}

if (source_col != "source") {
  da &lt;- da |&gt;
    rename(source = all_of(source_col))
}

da &lt;- da |&gt;
  mutate(
    source = case_when(
      str_detect(str_to_upper(as.character(source)), "MI") ~ "MI",
      str_detect(str_to_upper(as.character(source)), "OPW") ~ "OPW",
      TRUE ~ as.character(source) ), source = factor(source)) |&gt;
  arrange(st_id, time)

